fix(architecture): the successor of a discarded feature materializes its signed design

The prescribed recovery of a damaged Critic course is the PO's discard and a
successor feature with its own plan. The architecture receipt the discarded
feature left names its feature id and plan path: the refresh route needs the
same id and path, the inheritance route needs the predecessor in
closedFeatures, and the discard writes discardedFeatures. The signed
successor design therefore stopped at ARCHITECTURE-DESIGN-RECEIPT-STALE, and
a second signature could not change that classification.

A predecessor in discardedFeatures is now a lineage: its plan must still be
the one its receipt names, an equal design is inherited, and a changed
design (including a changed ownership) replaces the targets only over their
recorded bytes. Independent drift, an edited predecessor plan, a dropped file
that still exists and a predecessor in neither list are refused as before; a
closed predecessor keeps the additive rule.

